  "description": "telemetry.v2 §2.1 to §2.16: what a reader reads of a resource. `schema` is a packed document (core §7.6) whose record types the frame resources name. `resources` is the interface's other resources, each as telemetry.v1's declarations.json writes one (kind, annotations, type, attachment), with its `template` and `frame` (true for a frame resource); a template holds a parameter when it holds `{`. A case's resource is a frame resource (`frame` true: its record type, `record`, and its resolved annotations, given or merged from `layers` {defaults, kind_defaults, resource}, resource over kind_defaults over defaults) or any other (`frame` false: as telemetry.v1's declarations.json writes it, and expected as that file expects it). A frame resource's expect.declaration is one of: \"not_this_profiles\" (no telemetry.series, and none of telemetry.kind, unit, buckets, semantic); \"ignored\" (no telemetry.series, and one of those four); \"declared\", with `series`, one per entry in field order: `field`, `kind`, `unit`, `semantic` (each null when no entry gives it), `mirror` (the template it names, null inline) and `width` (a counter field's, else null); or \"invalid\", with `reasons`, each {entry, reason}: entry null for the annotation whole (series_value: not a table, or an empty one; nothing else checked), then each entry in byte order of its key, its reasons in this order: series_field (names no field), series_value (neither a string nor a table, or a table holding a member other than kind, unit and semantic; neither skips the rest), kind_value, unit_value, semantic_value (an inline member present whose value is not one, as telemetry.v1 §2.2 says), mirror_missing (the string names no resource of `resources`, or two, a frame resource, a template with a parameter, or a resource whose telemetry.v1 declaration is not_this_profiles or ignored), mirror_invalid (that declaration is invalid), kind_missing (an inline series with no kind, or a mirror declaring none), not_a_carrier (a kind given, and the field's type cannot carry it: counter on counter, gauge on int or fixed, boolean on bool, text on enum, nothing else). `contracts` reads each resource of a contract under `conformance/`, by its template: a frame resource's series as above, any other's telemetry.v1 declaration.",
